From 505849d93a26bc7bbcffb5fccc622a29bea3642c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Azra Bano <azrabano.work@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:41:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Jaeckel's "Let's Be Rational" Black implied standard
 deviation

Add blackFormulaImpliedStdDevLetsBeRational, which inverts the Black
formula to close to machine precision for any admissible price using
P. Jaeckel, "Let's Be Rational", Wilmott (2015), pp. 40-53: a rational
cubic initial guess on four segments of the normalised Black function
followed by at most two third-order Householder steps.

The normalised Black function, its inverse and the supporting special
functions (Cody's erfc/erfcx) live in the new letsberational.{hpp,cpp}
under QuantLib::detail. They are ported from Jaeckel's reference
implementation, whose notice is preserved in the source.

blackFormulaImpliedStdDev is unchanged.
